# ⚠️⚠️ STAGING NOINDEX MANDATE — one of THREE signals, re-asserted every build.
#
# The other two are `Disallow: /` in robots.txt and a `noindex, nofollow` meta
# tag from src/components/BaseHead.astro. They are deliberately in three places
# so that taking them off is a deliberate act, and taking them off is now
# exactly one deliberate act: `RP_TARGET=prod`. scripts/target-noindex.mjs
# removes this block on a production build and FAILS the build if it cannot
# find it, because a signal it could not find is a signal it cannot promise it
# removed. Cloudflare Pages also serves a platform noindex header on
# *.pages.dev, but that header is invisible from any config we control, so it
# is never relied on.
/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow

/images/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/_img/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/favicon.*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600, must-revalidate

/apple-touch-icon*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600, must-revalidate

# One block for the fonts, not two. Session replay runs in an iframe on the
# dashboard origin and web fonts are CORS-gated, so without the allow-origin
# header the client sees their own site in a fallback face. That header was
# added on 2026-08 in a SECOND `/fonts/*` block below the first one, which
# meant two rules for one path and no way to tell from the file which of them
# Cloudflare would apply. Merged 2026-11-11.
/fonts/*
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
